## Program Learning Outcomes

The program integrates advanced biblical studies, systematic theology, pastoral formation, and practical ministry from a Pentecostal–Charismatic perspective.

Students completing this program will be able to:

- Demonstrate advanced competence in biblical and theological studies.
- Interpret and communicate Scripture through sound exegesis.
- Explain Pentecostal–Charismatic theology and pneumatology.
- Demonstrate effective preaching, teaching, and pastoral leadership.
- Apply biblical principles to pastoral counseling and spiritual care.
- Understand the gifts, empowerment, and ministry of the Holy Spirit.
- Develop effective strategies for evangelism, missions, and church planting.
- Demonstrate spiritual maturity, Christian character, and ministry ethics.